  "id": "397b3be6-2a94-55af-9d3f-1d5c0b27bc26",
  "slug": "sweet-potato-sage-biscuits-recipe-8347363",
  "name": "Sweet Potato Sage Biscuits",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "This sweet potato\u2013sage biscuits recipe makes savory, honey-kissed biscuits that are buttery and moist with the addition of sage for an earthy flavor.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C). Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pierce potato several times with a fork. Microwave on High until tender, about 5 minutes. Scoop out flesh and mash when cool enough to handle. Measure 1 cup mashed sweet potato; reserve remaining potato for another use."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Whisk flour, sage, baking powder, baking soda, and salt together in a large bowl."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Coat stick of butter in flour mixture; grate on the large holes of a box grater into a medium bowl. If butter starts to melt, coat in flour mixture again and continue grating. Toss butter in flour mixture with fingers until butter pieces are separated and coated in flour; mixture should resemble coarse crumbs."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Whisk yogurt, milk, and honey in a medium bowl. Stir in potato; add to flour mixture. Gently fold to bring dough together; it should be moist but still crumbly. If dough is too dry, add cold water 1 tablespoon at a time."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Turn dough out onto a lightly floured work surface. Lightly knead three or four times until dough comes together. Sprinkle with flour; pat to 3/4-inch thickness. Cut dough into four equal portions. Stack portions, press down, and pat again to form a 3/4-inch-thick rectangle. Repeat process three times, adding flour as needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Press a 2 1/2- to 3-inch biscuit cutter straight down into dough to cut out biscuits. Gently knead scraps together, pat to 3/4-inch thickness, and repeat until all dough is used. Arrange biscuits on the prepared baking sheet."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until tops are golden brown, 16 to 18 minutes. Let cool on baking sheet 5 minutes. Brush tops with butter and sprinkle with flaky salt."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 18,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 15,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 25,
